# Python tooling
# Virtualenvs, under any name and at any depth. Neither pattern is anchored with a leading slash,
# so both match in every directory -- including the per-task checkouts under .claude/worktrees/,
# which is where the .venv312/ that got committed actually lived. The trailing slash keeps these
# matching directories only, so a file named e.g. venv_notes.md is still tracked.
.venv*/
venv*/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/